.TH BITBAKE-SETUP 1 "February 2026" 
.SH NAME
bitbake-setup \- BitBake setup utility and environment manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bitbake-setup
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIsubcommand\fR] [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bitbake-setup
is a utility to manage BitBake build environments. It allows for initializing 
configurations, managing layers, and ensuring host dependencies are met through 
buildtools.
.PP
Run with the \fBinit\fR argument to get started with a new configuration.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List available configurations.
.TP
.B init
Select a configuration and initialize a setup from it.
.TP
.B status
Check if the local setup needs to be synchronized with the configuration.
.TP
.B update
Update a local setup to be in sync with the current configuration.
.TP
.B install-buildtools
Install buildtools to fulfill missing or incorrect host dependencies.
.TP
.B settings
Manage settings files (prefix, directory names, registry locations, etc.).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show summary of options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable detailed debug output.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only errors; suppress status messages.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " COLOR"
Colorize output. \fICOLOR\fR can be \fBauto\fR, \fBalways\fR, or \fBnever\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no-network
Use only local cache; do not check for remote repository updates.
.TP
.BI \-\-global-settings " PATH"
Path to a specific global settings file.
.TP
.BI \-\-setting " SECTION SETTING VALUE"
Modify a specific setting for this invocation only.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B bitbake-setup init
.IP
Starts the interactive initialization process.
.PP
.B bitbake-setup --no-network update
.IP
Updates the environment using only locally available cached data.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bitbake (1)
.PP
Use \fBbitbake-setup <subcommand> --help\fR for detailed help on a specific command.
